From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:25:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kodi: take the enhancement layer scaler from the engine that
 renders

The enhancement layer upscaling setting decides two things that must
agree: whether the engine uses CB1 Master Reference's processing for a
picture (cb1_contract, latched when the engine starts), and the chroma
siting Kodi chooses for that picture, which read the setting again on
every frame. Changing the setting during a title therefore sited
pictures for one processing while the engine applied the other until
the next video.

The adapter now reads the setting once, before its engine starts, hands
the same value to the engine and answers the siting question from it
for as long as that engine lives. A new engine (the next video, or one
started again after a failure) reads the setting again, for both.

Reset() left CB1's refresh rule where the previous stream had stopped
(m_cb1Frames, m_cb1LastPts): the first picture of the next stream got
its refresh only if its timestamp happened to step back or jump. They
are cleared, so the first picture after any reset is a first picture.
